    {"dot": "rose", "title": "Access and moderation", "items": [
      "HTML uses sessions; REST supports tokens and sessions, with authentication required by default.",
      "Shared queries enforce post visibility, private profiles, active authors and blocks.",
      "WebSockets require an allowed origin and an active authenticated session.",
      "Admin actions hide reported posts/comments and record report resolution."
    ]},
    {"dot": "violet", "title": "Notification delivery", "items": [
      "Likes, comments and social actions call notify; self and blocked notifications are skipped.",
      "Save the notification first; publish its ID to the recipient group only after commit and an eligibility check.",
      "The consumer rechecks visibility before sending JSON; app.js updates the toast and unread count.",
      "A publish failure is logged while the saved inbox notification remains available."
    ]},
    {"dot": "amber", "title": "Configuration, not deployment status", "items": [
      "Local defaults: SQLite, filesystem media, in-memory channels and LocMem cache.",
      "DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL and USE_S3 select the configured alternatives shown above.",
      "Redis channels and cache use the same REDIS_URL when set; they are separate logical roles.",
      "Production guards require PostgreSQL, Redis and private S3 storage. No live deployment is asserted.",
      "Daphne serves ASGI; WhiteNoise middleware and manifest storage support static assets."
    ]}
  ]
